  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1218 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nMonday though Wednesday still appear to the be the hottest days in\nthe extended period, with little in the way of rain chances, even\nacross the northwest counties. The broad upper high stretching \nfrom the 4-corners region to the Gulf Coast will keep the monsoon \nmoisture and storm track well to our north and west. High \ntemperatures will continue to creep upwards and may reach Heat \nAdvisory criteria (105-110 degrees) from the Caprock Canyons area \neast through the Prairie Dog Town Fork of the Red River Valley \ninto portions of the Rolling Plains Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nThe medium range guidance tends to split into two camps starting\naround midweek. One camp (mainly GFS-based) shows the upper high \ncenter shifting father northwest to the 4-corners region, allowing\nfor some northwesterly flow to develop across the Southern High \nPlains and possibly drag a cold front into the area late Wed or \nThu. This would result in at least a modest cool down and a better\nchance for some precipitation for the second half of the week. \nHowever, the other camp (mainly ECMWF-based) keeps the upper ridge\ncentered closer to home and would tend to prevent the front from \nentering our area, maintaining the hot and dry conditions. The \nmean (which our current forecast reflects) favors maintaining the \nbroad ridge over NM and TX with the front staying off to our \nnorth. However, this pattern may still allow temperatures to back \noff just slightly beyond Wednesday, and convection along the \nfront may yet drive it farther south than the current consensus.",
